1
00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:13,058
Chicks in Chains - where they come from this is... Fun!

2
00:10:14,117 --> 00:10:20,117
Black Mama, White Mama is a action, crime,
thriller film directed by Eddie Romero.

3
00:15:21,176 --> 00:15:27,176
When two troublemaking female prisoners (one a revolutionary, the other a former harem-girl)
can't seem to get along, they are chained together and extradited for safekeeping.

4
00:20:28,235 --> 00:20:34,235
The women, still chained together, stumble, stab, and cat-fight their way across the
wilderness, igniting a bloody shootout between gangsters and a group of revolutionaries.

5
00:25:35,294 --> 00:25:41,294
Lee Daniels, played by Pam Grier.

6
00:30:42,352 --> 00:30:48,352
Karen Brent, played by Margaret Markov.

7
00:35:49,411 --> 00:35:55,411
Ruben, played by Sid Haig.

8
00:40:56,470 --> 00:41:02,470
Matron Densmore, played by Lynn Borden.

9
00:46:03,529 --> 00:46:09,529
Ernesto, played by Zaldy Zshornack.

10
00:51:10,588 --> 00:51:16,588
Warden Logan, played by Laurie Burton.

11
00:56:17,647 --> 00:56:23,647
Black Mama White Mama, also known as Women in Chains (US reissue title), Hot, Hard and Mean (original 1974 UK title) and Chained Women
(1977 UK reissue title), is a 1973 women in prison film directed by Eddie Romero and starring Pam Grier and Margaret Markov.

12
01:01:24,705 --> 01:01:30,705
The film has elements of blaxploitation.

13
01:06:31,764 --> 01:06:37,764
The movie was reportedly inspired by the 1958 film The Defiant Ones.

14
01:11:38,823 --> 01:11:44,823
Set in an unspecified Latin American country referred to only as "the island",
the movie was shot in the Philippines for budgetary purposes.

15
01:16:45,882 --> 01:16:51,882
The film explores themes of sexual abuse, women's prison,
prison escape, jungle, racial tension.

16
01:21:52,941 --> 01:21:58,941
The tone is emotional and intense.
